xcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["minimum wage","labour market","wage floor","restaurants"],"qpPage":5,"msPage":12,"ctxPage":3,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2021-nov-q7","p":6,"section":"C","questionNumber":"7","parentQuestion":null,"choiceGroup":"edexcel-a-p1-2021-nov-sec-c","marks":25,"questionText":"The national living wage, the minimum wage for 25-year-olds and over, is expected to rise to more than £10.50 an hour in 2024 compared with £8.72 in 2020. The wage does not apply to the UK’s self-employed and ‘gig economy’ workers. Some economists said the increase was ambitious. Business groups warned that employers in sectors such as social care could be hit hard. In large parts of the north of England the living wage has already reached two-thirds of local median earnings, said Professor Shackleton. Evaluate the disadvantages of a significant increase in the national living wage on a specific labour market, such as that for social care workers.","topics":["3-5-3-wage-determination","3-6-1-government-intervention"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["national living wage","minimum wage","labour market","social care"],"qpPage":30,"msPage":23,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p3-2021-nov-q1e","p":22,"section":"A","questionNumber":"1(e)","parentQuestion":"1","choiceGroup":"edexcel-a-p3-2021-nov-q1-choice","marks":25,"questionText":"Evaluate the microeconomic and macroeconomic effects of increased government intervention in an industry. Refer to HCWs or another industry of your choice.","topics":["3-6-1-government-intervention"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["government intervention","regulation","enforcement","industry"],"qpPage":5,"msPage":12,"ctxPage":2,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2020-oct-q6c","p":7,"section":"B","questionNumber":"6(c)","parentQuestion":"6","choiceGroup":null,"marks":10,"questionText":"Assess whether complete nationalisation of the rail industry might protect employees.","topics":["3-6-1-government-intervention"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["nationalisation","public ownership","rail industry","employees"],"qpPage":11,"msPage":14,"ctxPage":9,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2019-jun-q6e","p":2,"section":"B","questionNumber":"6(e)","parentQuestion":"6","choiceGroup":null,"marks":15,"questionText":"Discuss methods of government intervention to protect consumers within the utilities markets, such as energy and telecommunications.","topics":["3-6-1-government-intervention"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["regulation","consumer protection","utilities","energy","telecoms"],"qpPage":13,"msPage":16,"ctxPage":11,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2018-jun-q6b","p":1,"section":"B","questionNumber":"6(b)","parentQuestion":"6","choiceGroup":null,"marks":12,"questionText":"With reference to Extract A, discuss the likely effectiveness of ‘measures to open up and increase competition’ in the UK energy market.","topics":["3-6-1-government-intervention","3-4-7-contestability"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["competition","energy market","barriers to entry","regulation"],"qpPage":19,"msPage":12,"ctxPage":17,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2018-jun-q6c","p":1,"section":"B","questionNumber":"6(c)","parentQuestion":"6","choiceGroup":null,"marks":10,"questionText":"With reference to Extract B, assess how the regulation of energy suppliers’ profits is likely to affect consumers and suppliers in the energy market.","topics":["3-6-1-government-intervention","3-6-2-the-impact-of-government-intervention"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["profit regulation","price cap","energy suppliers","regulation"],"qpPage":19,"msPage":15,"ctxPage":17,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2017-jun-q6c","p":0,"section":"B","questionNumber":"6(c)","parentQuestion":"6","choiceGroup":null,"marks":8,"questionText":"Examine measures the government might use to restrict the m